                    {
                      "id": "0211878d-d4bb-4740-8519-07a7a9d4ffd9",
                      "text": "文档: Linked lists: ordered lists, in which each element has a reference to the next …",
                      "children": [],
                      "isExpanded": true,
                      "parentId": "31b3f86e-e062-479d-b137-4a201203e84d",
                      "data": {
                        "note": "**文档**\n\nLinked lists: ordered lists, in which each element has a reference to the next element.\n\nMost operations on linked lists take time proportional to the length of the list, because each\nelement must be traversed to find the next element.\n\n`List α` is isomorphic to `Array α`, but they are useful for different things:\n* `List α` is easier for reasoning, and `Array α` is modeled as a wrapper around `List α`.\n* `List α` works well as a persistent data structure, when many copies of the tail are shared. When\n  the value is not shared, `Array α` will have better performance because it can do destructive\n  updates.",
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute",
                          "文档"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f9fafb",
                        "color": "#6b7280",
                        "fontSize": 11,
                        "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": false,
                  "parentId": "f72ef01a-4bc5-4a74-96de-c10fda3a169d",
                  "data": {
                    "tags": [
                      "attribute-group"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f3f4f6",
                    "color": "#4b5563",
                    "fontSize": 12,
                    "shape": "round",
                    "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": true,
              "parentId": "4b888ba7-012e-4d9d-b918-f6d29b0dc558",
              "data": {
                "note": "**层** 陈述\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nType u → Type u\n```\n\n**文档**\nLinked lists: ordered lists, in which each element has a reference to the next element.\n\nMost operations on linked lists take time proportional to the length of the list, because each\nelement must be traversed to find the next element.\n\n`List α` is isomorphic to `Array α`, but they are useful for different things:\n* `List α` is easier for reasoning, and `Array α` is modeled as a wrapper around `List α`.\n* `List α` works well as a persistent data structure, when many copies of the tail are shared. When\n  the value is not shared, `Array α` will have better performance because it can do destructive\n  updates.",
                "tags": [
                  "declaration",
                  "陈述",
                  "inductive"
                ]
              },
              "style": {
                "background": "#f8fbff",
                "color": "#1e3a8a",
                "fontSize": 13,
                "borderColor": "#93c5fd"
              }
