                        {
                          "id": "ab02b8d1-b939-44b1-a6b3-095f534bb625",
                          "text": "签名: ∀ {α : Sort u} {β : Sort v} {a₁ a₂ : α} (f : α → β), a₁ = a₂ → f a₁ = f a₂",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "79503498-4795-4859-a829-82afd460d05e",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**签名**\n\n∀ {α : Sort u} {β : Sort v} {a₁ a₂ : α} (f : α → β), a₁ = a₂ → f a₁ = f a₂",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "签名"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "f58d6cb7-3355-4659-99a6-94e68346764c",
                          "text": "文档: Congruence in the function argument: if `a₁ = a₂` then `f a₁ = f a₂` for any (n…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "79503498-4795-4859-a829-82afd460d05e",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\nCongruence in the function argument: if `a₁ = a₂` then `f a₁ = f a₂` for\nany (nondependent) function `f`. This is more powerful than it might look at first, because\nyou can also use a lambda expression for `f` to prove that\n`<something containing a₁> = <something containing a₂>`. This function is used\ninternally by tactics like `congr` and `simp` to apply equalities inside\nsubterms.\n\nFor more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality)",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "46a0bf40-f5e2-4564-9478-976656e5429e",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "bdb92e99-5003-4a63-a9e9-21227516d6b0",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** theorem\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {α : Sort u} {β : Sort v} {a₁ a₂ : α} (f : α → β), a₁ = a₂ → f a₁ = f a₂\n```\n\n**文档**\nCongruence in the function argument: if `a₁ = a₂` then `f a₁ = f a₂` for\nany (nondependent) function `f`. This is more powerful than it might look at first, because\nyou can also use a lambda expression for `f` to prove that\n`<something containing a₁> = <something containing a₂>`. This function is used\ninternally by tactics like `congr` and `simp` to apply equalities inside\nsubterms.\n\nFor more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "theorem"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
