                        {
                          "id": "87a24b9d-63f1-46f1-be7f-9342d4e063b7",
                          "text": "签名: {α : Sort u} → {β : Sort v} → {r : α → α → Prop} → Quot r → (f : α → β) → (∀ (a…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "a95b4e12-0591-4f5c-9756-0e40e376b814",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**签名**\n\n{α : Sort u} → {β : Sort v} → {r : α → α → Prop} → Quot r → (f : α → β) → (∀ (a b : α), r a b → f a = f b) → β",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "签名"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "00192c67-f33c-4ffe-8249-c0d1b3af1c35",
                          "text": "文档: Lifts a function from an underlying type to a function on a quotient, requiring…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "a95b4e12-0591-4f5c-9756-0e40e376b814",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\nLifts a function from an underlying type to a function on a quotient, requiring that it respects the\nquotient's relation.\n\nGiven a relation `r : α → α → Prop` and a quotient's value `q : Quot r`, applying a `f : α → β`\nrequires a proof `c` that `f` respects `r`. In this case, `Quot.liftOn q f h : β` evaluates\nto the result of applying `f` to the underlying value in `α` from `q`.\n\n`Quot.liftOn` is a version of the built-in primitive `Quot.lift` with its parameters re-ordered.\n\n[Quotient types](lean-manual://section/quotients) are described in more detail in the Lean Language\nReference.",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "b12fac58-6538-45ef-a0de-3883a332692c",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "fbeb1a68-70ad-4f3a-bbdb-6b6210739c89",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → {β : Sort v} → {r : α → α → Prop} → Quot r → (f : α → β) → (∀ (a b : α), r a b → f a = f b) → β\n```\n\n**文档**\nLifts a function from an underlying type to a function on a quotient, requiring that it respects the\nquotient's relation.\n\nGiven a relation `r : α → α → Prop` and a quotient's value `q : Quot r`, applying a `f : α → β`\nrequires a proof `c` that `f` respects `r`. In this case, `Quot.liftOn q f h : β` evaluates\nto the result of applying `f` to the underlying value in `α` from `q`.\n\n`Quot.liftOn` is a version of the built-in primitive `Quot.lift` with its parameters re-ordered.\n\n[Quotient types](lean-manual://section/quotients) are described in more detail in the Lean Language\nReference.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
