                        {
                          "id": "0fb7504c-6f23-445d-982d-48700e13aafd",
                          "text": "签名: Sort u → Sort (max 1 u)",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "474a6725-a0f9-4969-85d0-3627a4d65573",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**签名**\n\nSort u → Sort (max 1 u)",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "签名"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "a86400c8-7dbd-43c8-a26e-0c0f600310ac",
                          "text": "文档: `Inhabited α` is a typeclass that says that `α` has a designated element, calle…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "474a6725-a0f9-4969-85d0-3627a4d65573",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\n`Inhabited α` is a typeclass that says that `α` has a designated element,\ncalled `(default : α)`. This is sometimes referred to as a \"pointed type\".\n\nThis class is used by functions that need to return a value of the type\nwhen called \"out of domain\". For example, `Array.get! arr i : α` returns\na value of type `α` when `arr : Array α`, but if `i` is not in range of\nthe array, it reports a panic message, but this does not halt the program,\nso it must still return a value of type `α` (and in fact this is required\nfor logical consistency), so in this case it returns `default`.",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "3c220a95-42de-4a05-a34d-78cb38d6e2a8",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "d518726e-6f41-4085-8f7d-4667fac24d45",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 内部\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nSort u → Sort (max 1 u)\n```\n\n**文档**\n`Inhabited α` is a typeclass that says that `α` has a designated element,\ncalled `(default : α)`. This is sometimes referred to as a \"pointed type\".\n\nThis class is used by functions that need to return a value of the type\nwhen called \"out of domain\". For example, `Array.get! arr i : α` returns\na value of type `α` when `arr : Array α`, but if `i` is not in range of\nthe array, it reports a panic message, but this does not halt the program,\nso it must still return a value of type `α` (and in fact this is required\nfor logical consistency), so in this case it returns `default`.\n\n**说明** equation compiler / recursor / match 管道，默认折叠。",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "内部",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f9fafb",
                    "color": "#6b7280",
                    "fontSize": 12,
                    "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                  }
                },
