                        },
                        {
                          "id": "7c3e9ade-3ee2-4169-8e81-da9945c05465",
                          "text": "文档: The identity function. `id` takes an implicit argument `α : Sort u` (a type in …",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "2979eb5c-604c-4a17-9920-cedb2faa04b3",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\nThe identity function. `id` takes an implicit argument `α : Sort u`\n(a type in any universe), and an argument `a : α`, and returns `a`.\n\nAlthough this may look like a useless function, one application of the identity\nfunction is to explicitly put a type on an expression. If `e` has type `T`,\nand `T'` is definitionally equal to `T`, then `@id T' e` typechecks, and Lean\nknows that this expression has type `T'` rather than `T`. This can make a\ndifference for typeclass inference, since `T` and `T'` may have different\ntypeclass instances on them. `show T' from e` is sugar for an `@id T' e`\nexpression.",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "0efc3788-ed21-4411-8e1b-79747ff3e00a",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "d518726e-6f41-4085-8f7d-4667fac24d45",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 内部\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → α → α\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe identity function. `id` takes an implicit argument `α : Sort u`\n(a type in any universe), and an argument `a : α`, and returns `a`.\n\nAlthough this may look like a useless function, one application of the identity\nfunction is to explicitly put a type on an expression. If `e` has type `T`,\nand `T'` is definitionally equal to `T`, then `@id T' e` typechecks, and Lean\nknows that this expression has type `T'` rather than `T`. This can make a\ndifference for typeclass inference, since `T` and `T'` may have different\ntypeclass instances on them. `show T' from e` is sugar for an `@id T' e`\nexpression.\n\n**说明** equation compiler / recursor / match 管道，默认折叠。",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "内部",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f9fafb",
                    "color": "#6b7280",
                    "fontSize": 12,
                    "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "5b7099be-cfc2-413a-b4c6-7f32bed67991",
